# OSMRoad configuration
#
# There are NO client-side environment variables. Everything the browser needs
# is either build-time (Vite) or served by the Worker.
#
# The AI query backend runs on Cloudflare Workers AI through the `AI` binding, so
# there are no provider credentials to manage at all: no service account, no API
# key, nothing to leak. See worker/index.ts and the `ai` block in wrangler.jsonc.

# ── Worker variables (wrangler.jsonc → "vars") ───────────────────────────────
# Override per environment with `wrangler secret put`/dashboard vars if needed.
AI_MODEL=@cf/qwen/qwen2.5-coder-32b-instruct
AI_FALLBACK_MODEL=@cf/meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct-fp8

# ── Local development ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `npm run dev` runs Vite alone: no Worker, no AI route, no R2. The app falls
# back to its offline NL2SQL parser and to files you drop in yourself.
#
# To exercise the Worker, the R2 samples and Workers AI locally:
#   npm run cf-dev          # builds, then `wrangler dev` on http://localhost:8787
#
# Workers AI is always executed remotely and incurs usage charges even in local
# development. R2/local bindings default to local simulations under `cf-dev`
# unless you set "remote": true on the binding in wrangler.jsonc.
